cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you used Manusights to review your manuscript before submission, please cite this software using the metadata below. Cite the version DOI for reproducibility; link the concept DOI when referring to Manusights in general."
type: software
title: "Manusights: AI Pre-Submission Manuscript Review"
abstract: "Manusights is a hosted AI service that reviews academic manuscripts before submission. The system performs three primary analyses: live citation verification against scholarly databases (CrossRef, PubMed, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar, bioRxiv, medRxiv) covering more than 500 million works; vision-based parsing of figures, micrographs, and image-embedded equations; and journal-specific desk-reject scoring against a target venue's editorial triage patterns. The deliverable is a structured diagnostic report intended to surface the structural, citation, and figure-trust risks that determine editorial outcomes before a manuscript reaches a reviewer."
